## Third-party content

The `ponytail*` files under `skills/` are redistributed verbatim and are not
covered by the copyright above. `skills/grill-me/SKILL.md` is original work
written for this bundle; the section below records what it replaced.

### `skills/ponytail*/SKILL.md`

Verbatim from [DietrichGebert/ponytail](https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail)
at tag `v4.10.0`, verified byte-identical. MIT, © Dietrich Gebert.

### `skills/grill-me/SKILL.md`

Original text written for this port. The DSH mechanics it drives — one question
per turn through `ask_user_question`, looking up what the codebase already
answers, the "what to grill" checklist, the closing summary — are the point of
the skill and are reproduced here in this bundle's own wording.

For the record, the earlier revisions of this file were not original. Version
`547a5c9` and before shipped the body of npm
[`dsh-grill-me@0.1.0`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-grill-me) (MIT,
© chensatan13) verbatim. That package's README credits
[RobMitt/grill-me-skill](https://github.com/robmitt/grill-me-skill), from which
seven sentences were verbatim; that repository carries **no LICENSE file**, so
it is "all rights reserved" by default. The `description` line above descends
from [mattpocock/skills](https://github.com/mattpocock/skills) (MIT, © 2026 Matt
Pocock), where the design-tree framing originates. That ancestry is why the
body was rewritten: the mechanism is unencumbered, the old prose was not.

### Original work

Only the DSH integration — `index.js`, `lib/`, `cordis.patch.yml`, `test/` — is
original work.
